      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;the-problem&#34;&gt;The problem&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Given an &lt;code&gt;m x n&lt;/code&gt; &lt;code&gt;grid&lt;/code&gt; filled with non-negative numbers, find a path from top left to bottom right, which minimizes the sum of all numbers along its path.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; You can only move either down or right at any point in time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Example 1:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    
    &lt;input type=&#34;checkbox&#34; id=&#34;zoomCheck-b25d8&#34; hidden&gt;
    &lt;label for=&#34;zoomCheck-b25d8&#34;&gt;
        &lt;img class=&#34;zoomCheck&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; decoding=&#34;async&#34; 
            src=&#34;images/minpath.jpg#center&#34; alt=&#34;alt image&#34; 
             /&gt;
    &lt;/label&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;Input: grid = [[1,3,1],[1,5,1],[4,2,1]]
Output: 7
Explanation: Because the path 1 → 3 → 1 → 1 → 1 minimizes the sum.
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Example 2:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
